{
  "topic": "How should bathos (bth) resolve workspace root and workspace-relative paths when invoked from inside a git worktree?",
  "prior_context": "bathos = single-researcher experiment-tracking CLI (bth, Python 3.12, Typer/DuckDB/PyArrow). Researchers run bth from git worktrees (e.g. <repo>/.claude/worktrees/<name>/). Need correct behavior when invocation dir is a worktree, not the main checkout.\n\nRECON GROUND TRUTH:\n- find_project_config (config.py:27-34) walks [cwd,*parents] for first .bth.toml; reaches one from a worktree (each worktree has its own checked-in copy). Works.\n- capture_git_state (git.py:18-39) uses git rev-parse HEAD / --abbrev-ref HEAD / status --porcelain w/ cwd; git auto-resolves .git-file pointer, so branch/hash/dirty are correctly per-worktree. Good.\n- _require_project_slug (cli.py:44-54): BTH_PROJECT_SLUG env else [project] slug from .bth.toml => SAME slug across worktrees. Probably desirable.\n- _catalog_dir (cli.py:32-41): BTH_CATALOG_DIR env else [project] catalog_dir else default ~/.bth/catalog/ => SHARED GLOBAL by default. Cool-tier atomic write-then-rename is SLURM-safe but same-machine concurrent 2-worktree writes UNTESTED => latent race.\n- Sidecar (sidecar.py:206-209 + prereg.py:106-112): finds <stem>.bth.toml adjacent then p.resolve(); worktree is real dir => resolves worktree-local. Works.\n- CORE GAP: .bth.toml carries absolute [project] root (config.py:37-48). compact.py:402,410-415 & cli.py:1532-1537 set workspace_root = project_config.root; postmortem.py:104 validates asset links vs workspace_root. So postmortem/asset validation from a worktree checks the MAIN checkout, not the worktree's files. Concrete bug.\n- 'workspace' is NOT first-class in bathos (means 'project root' in postmortem; 'install level' in export.py). No entity to extend.\n- Schema v7 (schema.py:10); COOL_SCHEMA schema.py:33-77; Run dataclass schema.py:128-150; migrate.py:25-93 backfills columns. Adding a field is supported.\n- Test gaps: nothing exercises invocation from .claude/worktrees/, concurrent 2-worktree catalog writes, or recorded-root-vs-live divergence.\n\nDESIGN TENSIONS (probe, do not resolve in divergence): recorded [project] root (stable identity) vs live worktree path (correct file resolution) and WHICH operations bind to WHICH; worktree detection (git --git-dir != --git-common-dir, or --show-toplevel, or .git-is-a-file); tag runs with worktree identity vs branch-is-enough; catalog shared vs per-worktree-namespaced vs concurrency-hardened; backward compat w/ existing absolute-root sidecars + existing catalogs + v7 migration; minimal surgical fix vs first-class workspace abstraction; who consumes workspace_root beyond postmortem (sidecar/sync/export).\n\nHuman is away; facilitator proceeds autonomously, self-answering framing questions and honoring probe-only divergence."
